==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} ''[[superbus]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/suˈpɝb/|/səˈpɝb/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/sjuːˈpɜːb/|/suːˈpɜːb/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-superb.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(ɹ)b|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|su|perb|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# [[first-rate|First-rate]]; of the highest quality; exceptionally good.
#: {{ux|en|This champagne is '''superb'''.}}
#* {{RQ:EHough PrqsPrc|I|0105}}
#*: Captain Edward Carlisle{{...}}felt a curious sensation of helplessness seize upon him as he met her steady gaze,{{nb...}}; he could not tell what this prisoner might do. He cursed the fate which had assigned such a duty, cursed especially that fate which forced a gallant soldier to meet so '''superb''' a woman as this under handicap so hard.
# Grand; magnificent; august; stately.
#: {{ux|en|a '''superb''' edifice;&emsp; a '''superb''' colonnade}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} [[haughty|Haughty]].
#* '''1858''', {{w|Julia Kavanagh}}, ''Adèle, a Tale: Volume 2'' (p.235):
#*: A remark which Isabella received with a '''superb''' curl of the lip, but at the same time, and to her brother's infinite relief, she walked away.

